{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/776373-demonic-investments-and-the-fallen","id":776373,"title":"Demonic investments and The Fallen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-28T19:31:06-08:00","id":776373,"title":"Demonic investments and The Fallen","content":"Anyone else look at the &quot;Deal&quot; mechanics for thralls in Demon the fallen as apposed to Demonic investments and think &quot;man these guy's really got the short end of the stick&quot;?<br /> <br /> I mean I personally ignored it in favor of a system where it was basically the demonic investments system, but it it cost the demon a number of faith to give an investment to their thrall equal to it's investment rating. A demon could get a number of faith points from their thralls per day equal to half their permanent faith rounded up, and could &quot;ravage&quot; the rest once a day for a desperate evocation.<br /> <br /> It didn't overly effect game-play much as it meant the young slayer with only one thrall wasn't going to waste a months worth of saved faith just to give her charge super speed, yet also meant that enemy thralls were an actual formidable threats if they came from powerful demons with their own cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T13:33:31-08:00","id":777895,"title":"","content":"I was never really big on DtF, mostly because we really didnt have group of player in the area here that were into it. From what I read though it was more like when the demon takes on a host body they can't do the things that they used. I think using a Pact system like they have in Dark Ages Changeling may be suitable though, that is the system I use for spirit pacts in my WtA games (which includes 'Demons'; i consider them spirits in my games)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}